# Version control exists here for ONE reason: on 2026-08-03 an agent's edit sliced
# world/items/HUMAN-REFERENCE.md from a heading to end of file, 1,655 lines -> 538.
# There was no git, no backup, and the content was not recoverable from the
# transcript. Sections 000 and 1-7 -- the layer map, the LOD table, and the
# amplitude/frequency traps and guard rails, i.e. the "how to build a figure"
# half -- are PERMANENTLY LOST.
#
# So: track the SOURCE and the REASONING. Do not track the artefacts, which are
# large, regenerable, and would make commits useless.

# Renders, blends, caches, bakes -- all regenerable, all enormous
*.blend
*.blend1
*.blend2
*.png
*.jpg
*.exr
*.npz
*.wav
*.flac
*.mp4
*.bphys
# `render/*`, not `render/`: git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY,
# so the battery source below could never be re-included while this said
# `render/`. Everything at the top of render/ is still ignored.
render/*
work/
sim/tmp/
# R2-2233: `tmp/` was untracked AND unignored, and `gitguard.py seed-inflight`
# claims the whole dirty set -- so 160 of the 304 paths in the 2026-08-07 seed,
# 53% of it, were scratch files. Every one of them was a future false refusal
# aimed at whoever next touched that name. 86 entries, 733 MB, ZERO tracked
# files, so ignoring it loses nothing and shrinks the next seed to a fifth.
# The lesson is not about tmp/: a lock that claims "everything dirty" inherits
# the tree's untidiness as policy, and the guard had no way to tell scratch
# from somebody's unfinished work.
tmp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Large generated data. The DOCS in docs/ are tracked; these are not.
docs/screen_presence*.json
docs/screen_presence*_objects.json
docs/*_points.npz
# R2-1099: `docs/beat_sheet.json` was ignored here, and that is the structural
# reason a beat-1 camera fix sat unpromoted for ten hours while FOUR *candidate*
# sheets sat tracked beside it. It is 157 KB, not "large generated data", and it
# is not merely an output — it is the input `build_camera_rig` and
# `build_car_anim` read. The versioned artefact must be the one that ships.
docs/collision_report.json
docs/placement*.json
docs/depth_probe.json
docs/instance_variety.json
docs/presentation_normals.json
docs/inventory_iter.json

# THE GATE BATTERY IS SOURCE, AND `render/` WAS SWALLOWING IT.
#
# This file's own header says the point of version control here is to track THE
# SOURCE AND THE REASONING, because an agent's edit destroyed 1,655 lines that
# were not recoverable. But `render/` and `work/` are blanket-ignored, and real,
# hand-written, heavily-reasoned source lives in both:
# render/world/assembly/r2/ holds assemble.py, probeA..probeK, lib_battery.sh,
# the three battery.sh files and make_controls.py -- the entire #53 gate battery
# and every control scene generator in the project.
#
# The consequence is not hypothetical. `git log` on any of them is empty, so
# "establish a baseline from committed state before you change anything"
# (R2-079) is structurally IMPOSSIBLE for the battery, and the destruction this
# file exists to prevent is exactly as possible there today as it was before git
# was introduced. The .blend/.png/.exr rules above still exclude the artefacts;
# these two lines let the SOURCE through.
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so every
# level has to be opened one at a time. Everything not named here stays ignored,
# and the *.blend / *.png / *.exr rules above still win over these.
!render/world/
render/world/*
!render/world/assembly/
render/world/assembly/*
!render/world/assembly/r2/
render/world/assembly/r2/*
!render/world/assembly/r2/*.py
!render/world/assembly/r2/*.sh
# The three directories below were named ONE AT A TIME, so v123 -- which holds
# verify_assembly8.sh, the script SHIPPING.md tells the reader to run, plus
# material_graph_census.py, material_graph_diff.py, path_diff.py and
# build_json_diff.py -- was still fully ignored and has no history at all.  That
# is the exact failure this file's header was written about, one directory over.
# The glob covers every vNNN batch from here on; the `*` line below still
# excludes everything in them that is not .py or .sh.
!render/world/assembly/r2/v12?/
!render/world/assembly/r2/v1??/
render/world/assembly/r2/v1??/*
!render/world/assembly/r2/v1??/*.py
!render/world/assembly/r2/v1??/*.sh

# THE ITEM GATE VERDICTS ARE A STAGE-1 BUILD INPUT, AND `render/*` ATE THEM.
# R2-4020, found by the sweep that followed R2-3961.
#
# `world/build_items.py::check_row()` reads `render/items/<item>/gate.json` and,
# because `require_gate_accepted` defaults TRUE, appends a FATAL unless it finds
# `"result": "ITEM_ACCEPTED"`:
#
#     gate verdict is None, not ITEM_ACCEPTED (read from ...). A placement
#     stage that ships un-accepted geometry makes the gate optional.
#
# So `rm -rf render/items/` does not degrade the world build, it STOPS it --
# exactly the position `work/r2_1211_rubber_tracks.json` was in, one directory
# over, and for the same reason: a blanket `render/*` written to exclude
# renders swallowed the evidence sitting among them.
#
# AND THEY ARE NOT REGENERABLE IN THE WAY THAT MATTERS.  `tools/item_gate.py`
# will write a gate.json, so "a script produces it" is true and beside the
# point: what it writes is the verdict of A NEW RUN.  This project's own
# `tools/r2_1381_rescore.py` says it plainly -- "`gate.json` files are the
# record of the run that produced them and are not edited after the fact".
# The 33 files here are the record of the runs that ACCEPTED THE SHIPPED
# GEOMETRY. Re-rendering cannot restore that; it can only replace it with
# something else that has the same name.  520 KB for 33 files, so the "large,
# regenerable artefacts" reasoning at the top of this file does not apply.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so every
# level is opened one at a time and immediately re-closed.  Nothing else under
# `render/items/` -- the gate renders, the crops, the EXRs -- becomes visible,
# and the *.png / *.exr / *.blend rules above still win inside it.
!render/items/
render/items/*
!render/items/*/
render/items/*/*
!render/items/*/gate.json

# Telemetry is generated from the spec, but it IS the single source of truth for
# motion AND audio and it has been wrong in ways that took a day to find. Track it.
!telemetry/telemetry.csv

# THE BAR'S OWN INSTRUMENTS WERE UNTRACKED.  R2-2821.
#
# `work/` is blanket-ignored above, and the two probes the film bar reads every
# one of its numbers from live in it:
#
#     work/lighting/measure_film_scene.py    the delivery format, the grade,
#                                            the lamp load, the frame range
#     work/r2100/measure_film_extra.py       the levelling identity, the camera
#
# So `git log` on either is empty, and the reason five of the bar's lines were
# decorative for four film generations -- `measure_film_scene.py` not emitting
# `resolution_x` -- is a change nobody could have bisected, reviewed or
# reverted.  That is the SAME failure this file's header is about (1,655 lines
# destroyed with no history) and the same one the `render/world/assembly/r2/`
# block above was written to close, one directory over.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so every
# level is opened one at a time and immediately re-closed.  Nothing else in
# `work/` -- gigabytes of blends, logs and scratch -- becomes visible.
!work/
work/*
!work/lighting/
work/lighting/*
!work/lighting/measure_film_scene.py
!work/r2100/
work/r2100/*
!work/r2100/measure_film_extra.py
